  "title": "Profile quarantine and impute student ages",
  "slug": "student_data_quality",
  "topic": "Data quality pipeline",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "prompt": "Return a dictionary of three DataFrames: null_counts (one row counting nulls in each original students column; empty input gives zeros), quarantined (original student rows whose age is null), and adults. To form adults, include students with a matching city record by unique id, fill null age using the mean of non-null ages from the original students input rounded to nearest integer with .5 rounded up, then retain age >=18. If every age is null, leave nulls unfilled. adults columns: id,name,age,city,code. Quarantined rows remain eligible for imputation.",
